      "problem": "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B),$ where \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/fc64ff98353bdf3a31424efdc15c643f905810b8c565adfb242022977cac5c1f.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/032ba760a133550709729624f124cc299662c38023da7446115bc66e17b6715c.svg)\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24.$",
